<li>
<p><strong>Apartment Building Rules</strong></p>
<p>
Finnish apartment buildings often have shared rules about quiet hours,
laundry rooms, saunas, and common spaces.
</p>
<p>Tip: Quiet hours are often around 10 PM-7 AM.</p>
</li>

<li>
<p><strong>Heating &amp; Winter Living</strong></p>
<p>
Finnish homes are designed for cold winters. Learn how heating,
ventilation, and winter maintenance work.
</p>
<p>
Tip: Avoid blocking ventilation vents and report heating problems.
</p>
</li>

<li>
<p><strong>Maintenance &amp; Repairs</strong></p>
<p>
Learn when to contact your landlord, building maintenance company,
or property manager.
</p>
<p>
Tip: Save your building's maintenance and emergency contact numbers.
</p>
</li>

<li>
<p><strong>Tenant Rights &amp; Responsibilities</strong></p>
<p>
Understand rental agreements, deposits, rent increases, and your
responsibilities as a tenant.
</p>
More information: <a href="https://kkv.fi/en/"> Finnish Competition and Consumer Authority (KKV) </a>

</a>
</p>
</li>

<li>
<p><strong>Shared Facilities</strong></p>
<p>
Many apartment buildings have shared saunas, laundry rooms,
storage spaces, and bicycle storage.
</p>
<p>
Tip: Ask your building manager about sauna and laundry room bookings.
</p>
</li>
</ol>
